ore/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:16:26-07:00","id":984511,"title":"","content":"I assume that there is a chance we would get something for the Wild West in Dark Eras 2 (Wild West Geist was a stretch goal)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:40:20-07:00","id":985813,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pistols at dawn!&quot; A challenge no vampire has ever issued at another ;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T22:03:59-07:00","id":985944,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of curious about what kind of specific information a Vampire: Wild West book or chapter would include.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting premise, though not one that seems like a natural match.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wonder if the OP has been reading <i>American Vampire</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T22:19:18-07:00","id":985948,"title":"","content":"I don't think we'll ever see anything too substantive because it's not the kind of environment that's particularly conducive to vampires. You might see the odd small group of outlaws or the single vampire haunting a wild west boom town, but any town supporting a whole coterie would be a place under a constant pall of fear.<br /> <br /> Any vampire who existed in the wild west would probably be pretty monstrous. Even with the transient populations, it would be next to impossible to keep their identity a secret, and maintaining touchstones would be an incredibly difficult endeavor. Moreover, vampires who tried to sustain themselves in that environment would be rare. The real question is, why would they? Vampires thrive in large, dense, urban settlements because that allows them to retain their anonymity and provides them with a larger herd to draw from. Travel, even in the modern day, is incredibly perilous for vampires. It would be much worse in the American West, with those long stretches of open, sun-bleached desert. The advent of rail lines would ameliorate that somewhat, but most vampires in the west would likely be nomadic by necessity.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it could be a <i>great</i> setting for wraiths, werewolves, and especially prometheans. Changeling could be a good fit as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:21:54-07:00","id":985981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/983827-wild-west-vampire?p=985813#post985813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pistols at dawn!&quot; A challenge no vampire has ever issued at another ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>And High Noon would be even more tense! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:27:05-07:00","id":985983,"title":"","content":"What about non-cowboy vampires? Presumably there are vampires amongst the native american tribes in the Old West. Do they even still have a Masquerade or do the natives all accept the existence of the supernatural and know there are vampires amongst them? Some groups even knowing and accepting a vampire as one of them, perhaps. Your Medicine Man likes to stay in his teepee in the day but so what - his rituals actually work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:17:33-07:00","id":986146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/983827-wild-west-vampire?p=985983#post985983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about non-cowboy vampires? Presumably there are vampires amongst the native american tribes in the Old West. Do they even still have a Masquerade or do the natives all accept the existence of the supernatural and know there are vampires amongst them? Some groups even knowing and accepting a vampire as one of them, perhaps. Your Medicine Man likes to stay in his teepee in the day but so what - his rituals actually work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely an interesting idea, but it also strikes me as a society that's too scattered to sustain more than a vampire or two in an area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:44:31-07:00","id":986399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/983827-wild-west-vampire?p=986146#post986146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely an interesting idea, but it also strikes me as a society that's too scattered to sustain more than a vampire or two in an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a large population, agreed. But vampires don't need that much ordinarily. A point a night which will take a mortal a couple of days to recover from. A tribe of a hundred people could support 1-3 vampires without much trouble. Sometimes a vampire needs more, but these are also the times when a vampire is more likely to be able to drain some enemy dry. A larger group of native americans, say a thousand, could support more or older vampires quite comfortably, imo. Once you're not trying to hide it and pick up people at night clubs without anybody noticing, it's a lot easier to estimate what population size can support what vampire count. (pun shamelessly intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:49:01-07:00","id":986680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/983827-wild-west-vampire?p=985813#post985813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pistols at dawn!&quot; A challenge no vampire has ever issued at another ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, high Humanity / low BP vampires could pull it off.<br /> Alternatively, just go with Navy rules on that duel (first one to die, loses) and see who bolts for safety and shade first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}